# Generated files are written with LF by their generator scripts. Without pinning them,
# a checkout on Windows (core.autocrlf=true) converts them to CRLF, and the next `--check`
# run compares CRLF-on-disk against LF-from-generator and reports the file as stale when
# its content is identical. That sends someone regenerating an already-correct file and
# committing 480 lines of pure line-ending churn.
#
# Scoped deliberately to the generated artifacts rather than `*.sql` — a blanket rule
# would renormalise all 612 migrations on the next checkout.
supabase/migrations/*_lab_test_catalog_v*.sql text eol=lf
docs/api/openapi.json                         text eol=lf
